<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaTerrain_DuneSeas.xml               Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-13
  ============================================================================

  V1 ROW 4, override 2 of 3.

  WHAT THE PLAYER SEES: the arid maps stop being a flat sheet of Sand with an
  occasional soft patch and become a dune sea. Wide, obviously wavy SoftSand
  fields that you walk slowly through, with hard Sand between them. Arid
  shrubland, which today has no dunes at all, gets them.

  ===========================================================================
  DESIGN INTENT FOLLOWED
  ===========================================================================
    design/Jawa/mods/required_mods.md:459
      "Desert terrain: terrain QUANTITY is already solved (Geological
       Landforms + Biome Transitions + Alpha Biomes + Vanilla Landmarks
       Expanded + Choose Biome Commonality + Map Designer). Gap = desert
       FLAVOR DENSITY (sand/salt/hardpan/dune variants) ..."

    design/Jawa/worldbuilding/setup_checklist.md:142-143
      "gap is desert DENSITY (sand/salt/hardpan variants)"

    design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biome_terrain_palette.md:212
      "| Soft Sand | SoftSand | none | 0, slows movement | Dune interiors |"

  The design names the gap as density and names SoftSand as the dune terrain.
  This file is that density change and nothing else. No new def, no new art.

    design/Jawa/concept.md §7
      "The world is a desert sea to cross, not a place to settle."

  Dunes that cost movement are that sentence expressed as pathCost. SoftSand
  is pathCost 14 against Sand's 4 (Core Terrain_Natural.xml:324 and :289), so
  widening the dunes genuinely slows a crossing. That is intended, and it is
  the one thing here with a gameplay cost rather than a purely visual one.

  ===========================================================================
  WHAT IS BEING CHANGED, EXACTLY
  ===========================================================================
  Core/Defs/BiomeDefs/Biomes_WarmArid.xml already ships one SoftSand patch
  maker per hot desert biome, and the ONLY number touched here is its lower
  threshold:

    Desert         :256-269   threshold min 0.65   ->  0.55
    ExtremeDesert  :405-417   threshold min 0.65   ->  0.50
    AridShrubland  no terrainPatchMakers node      ->  gains one

  Lower threshold = more of the perlin field clears the bar = wider dunes.
  Perlin output clusters around 0.5, so 0.65 is roughly the top sixth of a
  map and 0.55 is roughly the top third. ExtremeDesert goes further because
  it is the deep desert and it is already 100% Sand at every fertility
  (its terrainsByFertility is a single Sand row, -999 to 999, :398-404).

  ⚠️ These two numbers, plus AridShrubland's 0.70, are the whole tuning
  surface. Raise them back toward 0.65 to undo. Nothing else depends on them.

  ===========================================================================
  SAFETY
  ===========================================================================
  Desert and ExtremeDesert: the target node exists on disk, so the op is a
  Conditional whose test xpath is IDENTICAL to the Replace's xpath. The
  predicate [terrain="SoftSand"] is what makes it order independent with
  respect to the sibling file JawaTerrain_SaltPans.xml, which adds a SECOND
  <li> to the same terrainPatchMakers list. Whichever applies first, this
  xpath still selects exactly the SoftSand threshold and never the salt one.

  AridShrubland has no terrainPatchMakers node, so it is guarded on the
  container with match/nomatch, for the reason set out at length in
  JawaTerrain_SaltPans.xml. The two files guard it identically, so either
  order works.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Core: Desert. Widen the shipped dune field. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="Desert"]/terrainPatchMakers/li/thresholds/li[terrain="SoftSand"]/min</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="Desert"]/terrainPatchMakers/li/thresholds/li[terrain="SoftSand"]/min</xpath>
      <value>
        <min>0.55</min>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Core: Extreme Desert. The deep desert is the dune sea proper. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ExtremeDesert"]/terrainPatchMakers/li/thresholds/li[terrain="SoftSand"]/min</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ExtremeDesert"]/terrainPatchMakers/li/thresholds/li[terrain="SoftSand"]/min</xpath>
      <value>
        <min>0.50</min>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!--
    Core: Arid Shrubland has no dunes at all today. Give it some, kept off
    the fertile ground by maxFertility so the biome still reads as shrubland
    rather than as a second Desert.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AridShrubland"]/terrainPatchMakers</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AridShrubland"]/terrainPatchMakers</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>
          <perlinFrequency>0.05</perlinFrequency>
          <maxFertility>0.45</maxFertility>
          <minSize>13</minSize>
          <thresholds>
            <li>
              <terrain>SoftSand</terrain>
              <min>0.70</min>
              <max>999</max>
            </li>
          </thresholds>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AridShrubland"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <terrainPatchMakers>
          <li>
            <perlinFrequency>0.05</perlinFrequency>
            <maxFertility>0.45</maxFertility>
            <minSize>13</minSize>
            <thresholds>
              <li>
                <terrain>SoftSand</terrain>
                <min>0.70</min>
                <max>999</max>
              </li>
            </thresholds>
          </li>
        </terrainPatchMakers>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
